From ac2ecbda7bae358172c71b35669a3ee0524a6ef4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:00:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(media): expose transition library catalogue and
 previews

Add GET /transitions/library and
GET /transitions/library/{name}/preview.mp4 beside the built-in
transition list. The catalogue returns name, family, description,
duration_default and preview_url, sorted by family then name, with an
optional ?family= filter and no authentication, matching GET /transitions.

A preview is a 1.2 s, 360x640 join between two generated gradient cards
rendered on first request with the existing CPU-only ffmpeg path. The MP4
is cached under {TEMP_DIR}/transition_previews/<name>.mp4 and served from
there afterwards; the encode is written to a unique temporary file and
renamed into place so a partial file is never served. Names must exist in
the 248-entry registry, so path traversal and unknown names both 404.

TRANSITION_LIBRARY_API=off hides both routes. Rendering code is not
touched; the editor can adopt the catalogue separately.

Attribution: OpenCode (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free), lane-b/round3.
